# os-simple.manifest: our own simple Unix tools, to show how they are built.
#
# The ish shell (the kernel boots /ish as init) and the hand-written utilities at
# the root, plus the name-resolution config ping and nc read. A flat root on
# purpose: this image is the small, readable counterpart to os-real. Host paths
# are relative to the repo root (mkimage.sh cd's there).

file 0755 /ish build/ish/ish

exec-dir 0755 / build/utils

text 0644 /hello.txt hello, world\n
text 0644 /resolv.conf nameserver 10.0.2.3\n
text 0644 /hosts 127.0.0.1   localhost\n10.0.2.2    gateway\n10.0.2.3    dns\n10.0.2.15   rach2\n
